   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling Modern Slavery in Viet Nam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For the past decade, Vietnamese adults and children have been among the top three nationalities of those referred as potential victims of trafficking in the UK National Referral Mechanism. Despite the significant efforts to prevent and eradicate the TIP from Viet Nam, the risks of smuggling and trafficking continue, especially due to exacerbated socio-economic situation in country since the COVID-19 pandemic. To address this issue, IOM Viet Nam is executing an additional three-year phase to &#x201c;Tackling Modern Slavery in Viet Nam&#x201d; project, to implement a coordinated series of interventions across the three pillars of Prevention, Protection and Prosecution. Based on the results and lessons learnt from the previous phases and in line with the National Program on Human Trafficking Prevention and Combat period 2021-2025 with a Vision to 2030, IOM will work closely with both central government partners and key actors on the ground. Activities will be rolled out at the national level with a particular focus on hotspot communities in key provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
